# Compare the self-test's verdict lines.  Two of them end in a value that is
# different on every run (a freshly generated key pair, and the RNG draw), so
# their details are cut off and only the name + PASS/FAIL is kept; every other
# line carries a fixed test-vector digest and is compared in full.
/crypto selftest: ecdh-roundtrip/ { s/.*\(crypto selftest: ecdh-roundtrip [A-Z]*\).*/\1/; p; b; }
/crypto selftest: random / { s/.*\(crypto selftest: random [A-Z]*\).*/\1/; p; b; }
s/.*\(crypto selftest: .*\)/\1/p
